Scrutiny is a hard drive health dashboard and monitoring solution. It
combines S.M.A.R.T. metrics from smartctl with real-world failure rates
to warn of failing disks, and keeps a history of each disk's attributes.

This port installs two collectors from the Starosdev fork of Scrutiny,
which send data to a Scrutiny web server (hub) running elsewhere:

- scrutiny-collector-metrics reads the S.M.A.R.T. data of the local
  disks with smartctl
- scrutiny-collector-zfs reports the health and capacity of the local
  ZFS pools

The collectors must match the hub's version.
